# ── Ryne AI gateway (deploy on ryne1.genzdigitalstore.com) ────────────────────
# Copy to .env on the Ryne AI gateway app and fill the secrets. Same generic
# proxy-gateway/server.js as the other tools — only this .env differs.

PORT=3000
TOOL_KEY=ryne
TOOL_NAME=Ryne AI

TARGET_ORIGIN=https://ryne.ai
# Ryne's logged-in app/editor lives at /dashboard (tools at /pages/humanizer, etc).
DEFAULT_PATH=/dashboard
# Where an admin CAPTURE lease lands to log in fresh and save a session to the vault.
SIGNIN_PATH=/signup

GATEWAY_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://ryne1.genzdigitalstore.com
API_BASE=https://api.genzdigitalstore.com/api/crm/proxy/gateway

# MUST match the backend values exactly (same shared pair as the other proxy tools —
# copy from the API app's .env or any existing proxy gateway's env vars):
LEASE_SECRET=__SET_TO_BACKEND_PROXY_LEASE_SECRET__
GATEWAY_KEY=__SET_TO_BACKEND_PROXY_GATEWAY_KEY__

# If Ryne serves CSS/JS from a separate CDN/asset host that fails to load cross-origin,
# proxy it same-origin through the gateway, e.g.:
# ASSET_ORIGINS=https://cdn.ryne.ai
# Keep IDENTITY_SHIELD unset unless proven auth-safe (it can log token SPAs out).

# ── Account/logout shield (per-tool) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# ACCOUNT_SHIELD is ON by default: logout is never proxied (it would kill the shared
# vault session), and account/billing/subscription/settings PAGE loads show a friendly
# "managed by Gen Z" notice while their billing APIs are stubbed. This is auth-safe and
# does NOT redact session JSON. Set ACCOUNT_SHIELD=0 only if a tool's working area lives
# under one of those path words (prefer NAV_BLOCK_EXCLUDE to carve out just that path).
#   NAV_BLOCK_EXCLUDE=/settings/editor        # don't block this working-area path
#   NAV_BLOCK_EXTRA=/manage-account,/wallet   # also block these tool-specific paths
# Direct-URL blocking for account pages BLOCK_NAV_RE misses (it is segment-bounded, so
# "/account" is blocked but "/myaccount" is NOT). Fragments are substring-matched and shown
# via the same friendly sendAccountNotice() page HIX uses — no duplicate blocking system.
# Ryne's /account, /profile, /settings, /billing, /subscription, /plans are already blocked by
# BLOCK_NAV_RE and /logout by LOGOUT_RE; this only adds the my-prefixed aliases.
# NOTE: NAV_BLOCK_EXTRA also feeds the API stub, so do NOT add a fragment (e.g. "history")
# that appears in a tool API path or the editor's history call would be stubbed.
NAV_BLOCK_EXTRA=myaccount, my-account
# HIDE_SELECTORS: comma-separated EXACT CSS selectors for this tool's account/top-bar/
# avatar containers (shipped in the critical hide CSS before first paint + to overlay.js).
# NEVER include the editor / chat / upload / result area. Example:
#   HIDE_SELECTORS=header .user-menu, aside .account-card

# ── Session-expired / public-page protection (WriteHuman & Ryne) ──────────────
# This tool serves its PUBLIC "Log in / Sign Up" page at the default path with HTTP 200
# when the vault session is dead (no redirect to /sign-in), which is why an expired
# account showed the public page instead of the tool. DETECT_LOGGED_OUT=1 makes the
# gateway: if account cookies WERE attached but the main page still shows a logged-out
# shell (sign-in AND sign-up CTA, NO logout/account control), flag the account
# session-expired server-side and show a friendly "session expired" page instead of the
# public page. The backend verifier does the same at save/verify time (tools.js
# detectLoggedOut), so admin sees "session expired / needs login". Leave ON for this tool.
DETECT_LOGGED_OUT=1

# ── Account-switch fix: per-lease browser-storage reset (WriteHuman & Ryne) ───
# Ryne is a client-side token SPA: it caches the signed-in account (and often a bearer
# token it replays in an Authorization header) in localStorage/sessionStorage on THIS
# gateway origin. That storage survives an account switch, so after you update this
# account's vault cookies the next launch would inject the NEW cookies yet the SPA could
# reopen the OLD/invalid account from storage. RESET_STORAGE_ON_NEW_LEASE=1 clears storage
# exactly ONCE per lease (on the first page load of a fresh launch) so the latest saved
# cookies always define the account; within a session storage persists so the app works
# normally. Cookie-session tools (HIX/BypassGPT) don't need this. Leave ON for this tool.
RESET_STORAGE_ON_NEW_LEASE=1
# Account/profile/billing/logout HIDING + route blocking is already provided by the
# shared ACCOUNT_SHIELD (default ON, blocks /account, /billing, /settings, logout, etc.
# with a friendly notice) and the generic href/aria/avatar sweep. The selectors below
# only cover Ryne's TOP-HEADER bits the generic rules can't reach (Tailwind/Radix markup,
# no stable classes), targeted via STABLE hooks pulled from Ryne's own app bundle:
#   a[href="/dashboard"]:not(.inline-flex)        -> the "Dashboard" nav link (the global
#        KEEP_RE deliberately preserves "dashboard" for other tools, so it needs an explicit
#        per-tool rule here); :not(.inline-flex) keeps the logo (logo->tool, harmless) and the
#        exact match leaves the tool's "/dashboard?openAIReport=true" AI-report link working.
#   #coin-count, img[alt="ryne coin"]             -> the token/credit balance number + coin icon
#   .relative.ml-3.mr-1:has(img[alt="ryne coin"]) -> the whole credit pill + topup popover wrapper
#   div:has(> img[alt="User"]), img[alt="User"]   -> the account/avatar dropdown trigger (avatar +
#        name + chevron); hiding the trigger makes the Account/Logout/Topup menu unreachable.
# The MARKETING header (shown on /pages/humanizer and whenever the SPA renders logged-out,
# e.g. right after a cookie update) reuses the SAME header component; its right-side cluster
# carries the account dropdown when logged in and the Get started / Sign Up / Theme CTAs when
# logged out. Because this hiding is CSS, it applies in BOTH states on every load/lease, so a
# cookie update can never bring the full nav back. Marketing-header hooks (keep "Tools", which
# is a <div>, not an <a href>, so it is never matched):
#   .glass-effect li:has(a[href="/about"|"/blog"|"/pricing"]) -> About / Blog / Pricing nav items
#   .glass-effect .flex.justify-end.items-center              -> the whole right CTA/account cluster
#   button[aria-label="Toggle theme"]                         -> the theme toggle
#   #freeOptionTry                                            -> the Sign Up CTA (stable id)
# NONE of these touch Ryne's editor/humanizer/result area or the Tools dropdown. Uses the
# existing HIDE_SELECTORS mechanism (critical hide CSS + overlay re-apply) — no new system.
HIDE_SELECTORS=a[href="/dashboard"]:not(.inline-flex), #coin-count, img[alt="ryne coin"], .relative.ml-3.mr-1:has(img[alt="ryne coin"]), div:has(> img[alt="User"]), img[alt="User"], .glass-effect li:has(a[href="/about"]), .glass-effect li:has(a[href="/blog"]), .glass-effect li:has(a[href="/pricing"]), .glass-effect .flex.justify-end.items-center, button[aria-label="Toggle theme"], #freeOptionTry
